(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m1"] = E["hr-m1"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-1-2"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Emails that get answers","tr":"Cevap alan e-postalar","fa":"ایمیل‌هایی که جواب می‌گیرند"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can write a clear, polite request by email and reply to one.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda e-postayla net ve kibar bir rica yazabilecek, bir ricaya da cevap verebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی یک درخواست روشن و مؤدبانه با ایمیل بنویسی و به یک درخواست جواب بدهی."},"hook":{"en":"Ask for one clear thing, with a reason and a date. A busy reader answers what is easy to act on. Same request, two emails. One reads like an order; the other gets an answer.","tr":"Net bir şey iste, nedenini ve tarihini de söyle. Yoğun biri kolayca yerine getirebileceği şeye cevap verir. Aynı rica, iki e-posta. Biri emir gibi okunuyor; diğeri cevap alıyor.","fa":"یک چیز روشن بخواه و دلیل و تاریخش را هم بگو. آدم پرمشغله به چیزی جواب می‌دهد که انجامش آسان باشد. یک درخواست، دو ایمیل. یکی شبیه دستور است و دیگری جواب می‌گیرد."},"before":{"en":"Ask a colleague for two details by email, politely, with a deadline.","tr":"Bir iş arkadaşından e-postayla, kibarca ve bir son tarih vererek iki bilgi iste.","fa":"با ایمیل و مؤدبانه از یک همکار دو مورد اطلاعات بخواه و یک مهلت بگذار."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"Ask for one clear thing, with a date","tr":"Net bir şey iste, tarih de ver","fa":"یک چیز روشن بخواه و تاریخ هم بده"},"body":{"en":"A busy reader answers a request that is easy to act on. So say what you need, why and by when.","tr":"Yoğun biri, kolayca yerine getirebileceği bir ricaya cevap verir. Bu yüzden ne istediğini, nedenini ve ne zamana kadar istediğini söyle.","fa":"آدم پرمشغله به درخواستی جواب می‌دهد که انجامش آسان باشد. پس بگو چه می‌خواهی، چرا و تا کی."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Polite requests","tr":"Kibar rica kalıpları","fa":"درخواست مؤدبانه"},"steps":[{"en":"Direct and polite: Could you + base verb.","tr":"Doğrudan ve kibar: Could you + yalın fiil.","fa":"مستقیم و مؤدبانه: بعد از Could you شکل ساده‌ی فعل می‌آید.","ex":"Could you send me the list?"},{"en":"Softer, for an extra favour: Would you mind + -ing.","tr":"Daha yumuşak, ek bir rica için: Would you mind + -ing.","fa":"نرم‌تر، برای یک خواهش اضافه: بعد از Would you mind فعل با -ing می‌آید.","ex":"Would you mind sending me the list?"},{"en":"Softest, for a big request: I was wondering if you could + base verb.","tr":"En yumuşak, büyük bir rica için: I was wondering if you could + yalın fiil.","fa":"از همه نرم‌تر، برای درخواست بزرگ: بعد از I was wondering if you could شکل ساده‌ی فعل می‌آید.","ex":"I was wondering if you could confirm the date."},{"en":"Then say why or by when, so they can plan.","tr":"Sonra nedenini ya da ne zamana kadar olduğunu söyle ki plan yapabilsinler.","fa":"بعد بگو چرا یا تا کی، تا بتوانند برنامه‌ریزی کنند.","ex":"...by Friday, because the visa office closes early."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Opener","What follows"],"tr":["Giriş","Devamı"],"fa":["شروع جمله","بعدش چه می‌آید"]},"rows":[["Could you","base verb: send, confirm, check"],["Would you mind","-ing: sending, checking"],["I was wondering if you could","base verb"],["Email moves","purpose, request, deadline, close"]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish puts politeness inside the verb (gönderebilir misiniz) and Persian often says 'mishe ... befrestid'. In English the politeness is a separate opener and the verb stays bare.","tr":"Türkçede kibarlık fiilin içindedir: 'gönderebilir misiniz?'. İngilizcede kibarlık ayrı bir başlangıç kalıbıdır (Could you) ve fiil yalın kalır: send, to send değil.","fa":"در فارسی ادب معمولاً در خود فعل یا با «می‌شود ... بفرستید؟» می‌آید. در انگلیسی ادب یک عبارت جداست که اول جمله می‌آید (Could you) و فعل بعدش ساده می‌ماند: send، نه ⁨to send⁩."},"wrong":"Could you to send me the list?","right":"Could you send me the list?"},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"I was wondering if you could...","meaning":{"en":"Very polite request.","tr":"Çok kibar rica.","fa":"درخواست بسیار مؤدبانه"}},{"phrase":"Would you mind sending...","meaning":{"en":"Polite; followed by -ing.","tr":"Kibar; arkasından -ing gelir.","fa":"مؤدبانه؛ بعد از آن فعل ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید"}},{"phrase":"by the end of the day","meaning":{"en":"A clear deadline.","tr":"Net bir son tarih.","fa":"یک مهلت مشخص"}},{"phrase":"confirm","meaning":{"en":"To say that something is true or agreed.","tr":"teyit etmek.","fa":"تأیید کردن؛ قطعی کردن"}},{"phrase":"I'm writing to ask...","meaning":{"en":"Opening line that gives the purpose.","tr":"amacı belirten açılış.","fa":"جمله‌ی اولی که هدف ایمیل را می‌گوید"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Short emails: direct or cold?","tr":"Kısa e-posta: doğrudan mı, soğuk mu?","fa":"ایمیل کوتاه: رُک یا سرد؟"},"body":{"en":"Some workplaces, such as many in the Persian Gulf and in fast-moving logistics, write short, direct messages and do not mean to be rude. In the UK, very short emails can feel cold. When unsure, add one polite opener and one clear deadline.","tr":"Basra Körfezi'ndeki birçok işyeri ve hızlı lojistik sektörü gibi bazı ortamlarda kısa ve doğrudan mesajlar yazılır; bu kabalık anlamına gelmez. Birleşik Krallık'ta çok kısa e-postalar soğuk algılanabilir. Emin değilsen bir kibar giriş ve net bir son tarih ekle.","fa":"در بعضی محیط‌های کاری، مثل بسیاری از شرکت‌های حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس و شرکت‌های پرشتاب لجستیک، پیام‌ها را کوتاه و مستقیم می‌نویسند و قصد بی‌احترامی ندارند. در بریتانیا اما ایمیل خیلی کوتاه ممکن است سرد به نظر برسد. اگر مطمئن نیستی، یک جمله‌ی شروع مؤدبانه و یک مهلت روشن اضافه کن."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از دستور تا درخواست مؤدبانه"},"text":"Facts: You need the visa forms by Friday, to book the flights.","item":"Send the forms. Need them soon.","why":{"en":"Weak: cold, with no reason and no date. Strong: polite, with a reason and a deadline.","tr":"Zayıf: soğuk, nedeni ve tarihi yok. Güçlü: kibar, nedeni ve son tarihi var.","fa":"نسخه‌ی اول سرد است و نه دلیل دارد، نه تاریخ. نسخه‌ی دوم مؤدبانه است و دلیل و مهلت هم دارد."},"answer":"Could you send me the visa forms by Friday? I need them to book the flights.","cut":["soon"],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the word that gives the reader no real date.","tr":"Okuyana gerçek bir tarih vermeyen kelimeye dokun.","fa":"روی کلمه‌ای بزن که به خواننده تاریخ واقعی نمی‌دهد."}},"quick":{"prompt":"You write to a UK colleague you do not know well. Your whole email is \"Send the list by Friday.\" What should you add?","options":["One polite opener","A later deadline","Nothing: short is always fine"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"One polite opener: in the UK a very short email can feel cold. The clear deadline can stay.","tr":"Kibar bir açılış cümlesi: İngiltere’de çok kısa bir e-posta soğuk gelebilir. Net son tarih kalabilir.","fa":"یک جمله‌ی شروع مؤدبانه: در انگلیس ایمیلِ خیلی کوتاه ممکن است سرد به نظر برسد. مهلت روشن می‌تواند بماند."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Cover the opener. Is it 'send me the list' or 'sending me the list'? Could you takes the first, Would you mind the second. Result of this lesson: you can write a polite request that gets an answer. You also have a reply to a short email.","tr":"Başlangıç kalıbını kapat. 'send me the list' mi, 'sending me the list' mi? Could you birincisini, Would you mind ikincisini alır. Bu dersin sonucu: cevap alan kibar bir rica yazabilirsin ve elinde çok kısa bir e-postaya yazılmış cevabın olur.","fa":"اول جمله را بپوشان. «send me the list» است یا «sending me the list»؟ Could you اولی را می‌گیرد و Would you mind دومی را. حالا می‌توانی درخواستی مؤدبانه بنویسی که جواب بگیرد. جواب یک ایمیل خیلی کوتاه هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"Softer requests: I would appreciate it if...","tr":"Daha yumuşak ricalar: I would appreciate it if...","fa":"درخواست نرم‌تر: I would appreciate it if..."},"steps":[{"en":"I would appreciate it if you could + verb.","tr":"I would appreciate it if you could + fiil.","fa":"بعد از I would appreciate it if you could فعل ساده می‌آید.","ex":"I would appreciate it if you could send it by Friday."},{"en":"Would it be possible to + verb?","tr":"Would it be possible to + fiil?","fa":"بعد از Would it be possible to هم فعل ساده می‌آید.","ex":"Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?"},{"en":"I was hoping you could + verb: soft and warm.","tr":"I was hoping you could + fiil: yumuşak ve sıcak.","fa":"I was hoping you could هم با فعل ساده می‌آید و لحنش نرم و گرم است.","ex":"I was hoping you could check the dates."}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["I would appreciate it if you could...","I would appreciate it if you could send the list by Friday."],["Would it be possible to...?","Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?"],["I was hoping you could...","I was hoping you could check the dates."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: your reply to Omar must include one of the three softer patterns.","tr":"B2 yolu: Omar'a yanıtında üç yumuşak kalıptan biri mutlaka olmalı.","fa":"مسیر B2: جوابت به عمر باید دست‌کم یکی از این سه الگوی مؤدبانه را داشته باشد."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","title":"Polite requests","titleTr":"Kibar rica kalıpları","exp":{"en":"A polite request softens the order. The three safest openers are \"Could you...?\", \"Would you mind...?\" and \"I was wondering if you could...\". After \"Could you\" the verb is the base form with no \"to\": \"Could you send me the list?\" After \"Would you mind\" use -ing: \"Would you mind sending me the list?\". After \"I was wondering if\" the rest is a normal statement: \"I was wondering if you could confirm the date.\" Add a reason or a deadline to help the reader act: \"...by Friday, because the visa office closes early.\" A bare \"Need 3 drivers ASAP\" is clear but cold.","tr":"Kibar bir rica emri yumuşatır. En güvenli üç kalıp: \"Could you...?\", \"Would you mind...?\" ve \"I was wondering if you could...\". \"Could you\" sonrasında fiil yalın hâldedir, \"to\" gelmez: \"Could you send me the list?\". \"Would you mind\" sonrasında -ing gelir: \"Would you mind sending me the list?\". \"I was wondering if\" sonrasında cümle düz cümle olur: \"I was wondering if you could confirm the date.\" Okuyanın harekete geçmesi için bir sebep ya da son tarih ekle: \"...by Friday, because the visa office closes early.\" Sadece \"Need 3 drivers ASAP\" açıktır ama soğuktur.","fa":"درخواست مؤدبانه از تندی دستور کم می‌کند. سه شروعِ مطمئن برای درخواست این‌هاست: «⁨Could you...?⁩»، «⁨Would you mind...?⁩» و «⁨I was wondering if you could...⁩». بعد از ⁨Could you⁩ فعل به شکل ساده و بدون ⁨to⁩ می‌آید: «⁨Could you send me the list?⁩» بعد از ⁨Would you mind⁩ فعل ⁨-ing⁩ می‌گیرد: «⁨Would you mind sending me the list?⁩» بعد از ⁨I was wondering if⁩، بقیه‌ی جمله یک جمله‌ی خبری معمولی است، نه سؤالی: «⁨I was wondering if you could confirm the date.⁩» اگر یک دلیل یا یک مهلت هم اضافه کنی، خواننده راحت‌تر دست به کار می‌شود: «⁨...by Friday, because the visa office closes early.⁩» پیامی مثل «⁨Need 3 drivers ASAP⁩» روشن است، اما سرد و دستوری به نظر می‌رسد."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Opener","What follows"],"tr":["Giriş","Devamı"],"fa":["شروع جمله","بعدش چه می‌آید"]},"rows":[["Could you","base verb: send, confirm, check"],["Would you mind","-ing: sending, checking"],["I was wondering if you could","base verb"],["Email moves","purpose, request, deadline, close"]]},"wrong":"Could you to send me the driver list?","right":"Could you send me the driver list?","blank":{"sentence":"Could you ___ me the driver list by Friday?","word":"send","distractors":["to send","sending"]},"wrong2":"Would you mind to send me the list?","right2":"Would you mind sending me the list?","blank2":{"sentence":"I was wondering ___ you could confirm the date.","word":"if","distractors":["that","what"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"Same request, two emails. One reads like an order; the other gets an answer.","tr":"Aynı rica, iki e-posta. Biri emir gibi okunuyor; diğeri cevap alıyor.","fa":"یک درخواست، دو ایمیل. یکی شبیه دستور است و دیگری جواب می‌گیرد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"send: after 'Could you' the verb stays bare. 'Could you to send' is the error we see most.","tr":"send: 'Could you'dan sonra fiil yalın kalır. En sık gördüğümüz hata 'Could you to send'.","fa":"جواب send است: بعد از Could you فعل به شکل ساده می‌ماند. رایج‌ترین خطا Could you to send است."},"rule":[{"en":"Could you + bare verb.","tr":"Could you + yalın fiil.","fa":"بعد از Could you شکل ساده‌ی فعل می‌آید.","ex":"Could you send me the list?"},{"en":"Would you mind + -ing.","tr":"Would you mind + -ing.","fa":"بعد از Would you mind فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"Would you mind sending me the list?"},{"en":"I was wondering if you could + bare verb.","tr":"I was wondering if you could + yalın fiil.","fa":"بعد از I was wondering if you could شکل ساده‌ی فعل می‌آید.","ex":"I was wondering if you could confirm the date."},{"en":"Then say why or by when.","tr":"Sonra nedenini ya da ne zamana kadar olduğunu söyle.","fa":"بعد بگو چرا، یا تا کی.","ex":"...by Friday, because the visa office closes early."}],"test":{"en":"Cover the opener. Is it 'send me the list' or 'sending me the list'? Could you takes the first, Would you mind the second.","tr":"Başlangıç kalıbını kapat. 'send me the list' mi, 'sending me the list' mi? Could you birincisini, Would you mind ikincisini alır.","fa":"اول جمله را بپوشان. «send me the list» است یا «sending me the list»؟ Could you اولی را می‌گیرد و Would you mind دومی را."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish puts politeness inside the verb (gönderebilir misiniz) and Persian often says 'mishe ... befrestid'. In English the politeness is a separate opener and the verb stays bare.","tr":"Türkçede kibarlık fiilin içindedir: 'gönderebilir misiniz?'. İngilizcede kibarlık ayrı bir başlangıç kalıbıdır (Could you) ve fiil yalın kalır: send, to send değil.","fa":"در فارسی ادب معمولاً در خود فعل یا با «می‌شود ... بفرستید؟» می‌آید. در انگلیسی ادب یک عبارت جداست که اول جمله می‌آید (Could you) و فعل بعدش ساده می‌ماند: send، نه ⁨to send⁩."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["could you to","can you to","would you to"],"fix":{"en":"After could you / can you the verb has no 'to': 'Could you send me the list?'","tr":"could you / can you'dan sonra fiil 'to' almaz: 'Could you send me the list?'","fa":"بعد از could you یا can you فعل to نمی‌گیرد: «⁨Could you send me the list?⁩»"}},{"find":["would you mind to","do you mind to"],"fix":{"en":"After would you mind use -ing: 'Would you mind sending me the list?'","tr":"would you mind'dan sonra -ing kullan: 'Would you mind sending me the list?'","fa":"بعد از ⁨would you mind⁩ فعل ⁨-ing⁩ بیاور: «⁨Would you mind sending me the list?⁩»"}},{"find":["i was wondering could you","i was wondering can you","i was wondering that you"],"fix":{"en":"Use 'I was wondering if you could...' and keep the normal word order after it.","tr":"'I was wondering if you could...' kullan ve ardından düz cümle sırasını koru.","fa":"بنویس «⁨I was wondering if you could...⁩» و بعدش ترتیب جمله‌ی خبری را نگه دار."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","title":"Softer requests: I would appreciate it if...","titleTr":"Daha yumuşak ricalar: I would appreciate it if...","exp":{"en":"At B2 you can make a request softer and more formal with a few fixed patterns: \"I would appreciate it if you could send the list by Friday.\", \"Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?\", \"I was hoping you could check the dates.\" Two traps. First, appreciate needs an object: \"I would appreciate it if...\", not \"I would appreciate if...\". Second, after \"Would it be possible\" use to + verb: \"to move\", not \"moving\" or \"that move\". Use these with senior people, clients and anyone you are asking for a favour; with close colleagues, could is enough.","tr":"B2 düzeyinde birkaç kalıpla ricayı daha yumuşak ve resmî yapabilirsin: \"I would appreciate it if you could send the list by Friday.\", \"Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?\", \"I was hoping you could check the dates.\" İki tuzak var. Birincisi, appreciate bir nesne ister: \"I would appreciate it if...\"; \"I would appreciate if...\" değil. İkincisi, \"Would it be possible\" kalıbından sonra to + fiil gelir: \"to move\"; \"moving\" ya da \"that move\" değil. Bu kalıpları üst düzey kişilerle, müşterilerle ve bir iyilik istediğin herkesle kullan; yakın iş arkadaşlarıyla could yeterlidir.","fa":"در سطح B2 می‌توانی با چند الگوی ثابت، درخواستت را نرم‌تر و رسمی‌تر کنی: «⁨I would appreciate it if you could send the list by Friday.⁩»، «⁨Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?⁩» و «⁨I was hoping you could check the dates.⁩» حواست به دو تله باشد. اول اینکه appreciate بدون مفعول نمی‌آید؛ پس «⁨I would appreciate it if...⁩» درست است، نه «⁨I would appreciate if...⁩». دوم اینکه بعد از Would it be possible از to + فعل استفاده می‌شود: «to move»، نه «moving» و نه «that move». این الگوها را با مدیران ارشد، مشتری‌ها و هر کسی که از او لطفی می‌خواهی به کار ببر؛ با همکاران نزدیک همان could کافی است."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["I would appreciate it if you could...","I would appreciate it if you could send the list by Friday."],["Would it be possible to...?","Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?"],["I was hoping you could...","I was hoping you could check the dates."]]},"wrong":"I would appreciate if you could send the list.","right":"I would appreciate it if you could send the list.","blank":{"sentence":"I would appreciate ___ if you could send the list by Friday.","word":"it","distractors":["that","so"]},"wrong2":"Would it be possible moving the call to Thursday?","right2":"Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?","blank2":{"sentence":"Would it be possible ___ the call to Thursday?","word":"to move","distractors":["moving","that move"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: your reply to Omar must include one of the three softer patterns.","tr":"B2 yolu: Omar'a yanıtında üç yumuşak kalıptan biri mutlaka olmalı.","fa":"مسیر B2: جوابت به عمر باید دست‌کم یکی از این سه الگوی مؤدبانه را داشته باشد."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-1-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"I would appreciate it ___ you could reply by Thursday.","options":["that","if","so"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"if: 'I would appreciate it if you could...' is the fixed polite form. 'That' and 'so' break it.","tr":"if: 'I would appreciate it if you could...' sabit kibar kalıptır. 'That' ve 'so' kalıbı bozar.","fa":"if درست است، چون I would appreciate it if you could الگوی ثابت و مؤدبانه است. that و so الگو را خراب می‌کنند."},"hint2":{"en":"After I would appreciate it, the request is a condition. Which word starts a condition?","tr":"I would appreciate it’dan sonra rica bir koşul olarak gelir. Koşulu hangi kelime başlatır?","fa":"بعد از ⁨I would appreciate it⁩، درخواست به شکل شرط می‌آید. کدام کلمه شرط را شروع می‌کند؟"}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"Ms Clarke is a client, not a colleague. Leyla needs a request that sounds even softer.","tr":"Ms Clarke bir müşteri, iş arkadaşı değil. Leyla'nın daha da yumuşak bir ricaya ihtiyacı var.","fa":"خانم کلارک مشتری است، نه همکار. لیلا به درخواستی نرم‌تر از همیشه نیاز دارد."},"tryWhy":{"en":"to move: after 'Would it be possible' use to + verb, never -ing or that.","tr":"to move: 'Would it be possible'dan sonra to + fiil gelir; -ing ya da that gelmez.","fa":"جواب to move است: بعد از Would it be possible همیشه to و فعل می‌آید، نه -ing و نه that."},"rule":[{"en":"I would appreciate it if you could + verb.","tr":"I would appreciate it if you could + fiil.","fa":"بعد از I would appreciate it if you could فعل ساده می‌آید.","ex":"I would appreciate it if you could send it by Friday."},{"en":"Would it be possible to + verb?","tr":"Would it be possible to + fiil?","fa":"بعد از Would it be possible to هم فعل ساده می‌آید.","ex":"Would it be possible to move the call to Thursday?"},{"en":"I was hoping you could + verb: soft and warm.","tr":"I was hoping you could + fiil: yumuşak ve sıcak.","fa":"I was hoping you could هم با فعل ساده می‌آید و لحنش نرم و گرم است.","ex":"I was hoping you could check the dates."}],"test":{"en":"Did you write 'appreciate'? Look for 'it' right after it. No it? Add it.","tr":"'appreciate' yazdın mı? Hemen ardından 'it' var mı bak. Yoksa ekle.","fa":"appreciate نوشتی؟ ببین it بلافاصله بعدش آمده یا نه. اگر نیامده، اضافه‌اش کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'gönderirseniz memnun olurum' and the Persian 'mamnun mishavam agar...' have no object, so 'I would appreciate if' feels right. English appreciate always needs an object: it.","tr":"'Gönderirseniz memnun olurum' cümlesinde nesne yoktur, bu yüzden 'I would appreciate if' doğru gibi gelir. İngilizcede appreciate her zaman nesne ister: it.","fa":"در «ممنون می‌شوم اگر ... بفرستید» مفعولی نیست؛ برای همین «I would appreciate if» درست به نظر می‌رسد. در انگلیسی appreciate همیشه مفعول می‌خواهد: ⁨it⁩."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["appreciate if","appreciate that you could"],"fix":{"en":"appreciate needs 'it': 'I would appreciate it if you could...'","tr":"appreciate 'it' ister: 'I would appreciate it if you could...'","fa":"appreciate به it نیاز دارد: «⁨I would appreciate it if you could...⁩»"}},{"find":["would it be possible moving","would it be possible that","is it possible moving"],"fix":{"en":"Use to + verb: 'Would it be possible to move the call?'","tr":"to + fiil kullan: 'Would it be possible to move the call?'","fa":"بعد از Would it be possible از to و فعل استفاده کن: «Would it be possible to move the call?»"}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Email Phrases","tr":"E-posta Kalıpları","fa":"عبارت‌های کاربردی ایمیل"},"cards":[{"word":"I'm writing to ask...","sentence":"I'm writing to ask about the start date.","gap":"I'm writing to ask","accept":["i'm writing to ask","i am writing to ask"],"meaning":{"en":"Opening line that gives the purpose.","tr":"amacı belirten açılış.","fa":"جمله‌ی اولی که هدف ایمیل را می‌گوید"}},{"word":"by the end of the day","sentence":"Could you reply by the end of the day?","meaning":{"en":"No later than tonight.","tr":"gün sonuna kadar.","fa":"تا آخر امروز؛ حداکثر تا امشب"}},{"word":"urgent","sentence":"This request is urgent because the visa closes Friday.","meaning":{"en":"Needing action very soon.","tr":"acil.","fa":"فوری؛ چیزی که باید زود به آن رسیدگی شود"}},{"word":"attach","sentence":"I've attached the list of candidates.","gap":"attached","accept":["attached","attach"],"meaning":{"en":"To add a file to an email.","tr":"eklemek (dosya).","fa":"پیوست کردن (فایل به ایمیل)"}},{"word":"confirm","sentence":"Could you confirm the date by Monday?","meaning":{"en":"To say that something is true or agreed.","tr":"teyit etmek.","fa":"تأیید کردن؛ قطعی کردن"}},{"word":"as soon as possible","sentence":"Please send the form as soon as possible.","meaning":{"en":"As fast as you can. Often written ASAP.","tr":"en kısa sürede.","fa":"در اسرع وقت؛ هرچه زودتر (اغلب به شکل ASAP)"}},{"word":"I'd appreciate it if...","sentence":"I'd appreciate it if you could reply today.","gap":"I'd appreciate it if","accept":["i'd appreciate it if","i would appreciate it if"],"meaning":{"en":"A polite way to make a request.","tr":"...yaparsanız minnettar olurum (kibar rica).","fa":"ممنون می‌شوم اگر...؛ روشی مؤدبانه برای درخواست"}},{"word":"follow up","sentence":"I'm following up on my email from Monday.","gap":"following up","accept":["following up","follow up"],"meaning":{"en":"To contact someone again about an earlier message.","tr":"takip etmek.","fa":"پیگیری کردن؛ دوباره سراغ موضوعی را گرفتن"}},{"word":"Kind regards","sentence":"Kind regards, Leyla","meaning":{"en":"A polite way to end an email.","tr":"saygılarımla.","fa":"با احترام؛ با سلام و احترام (پایان ایمیل)"}},{"word":"blunt","sentence":"His email was blunt: only five words and no greeting.","meaning":{"en":"Direct in a way that can sound rude.","tr":"sert, patavatsız.","fa":"آن‌قدر رُک که بی‌ادبانه به نظر برسد"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","title":{"en":"Five Words","tr":"Beş Kelime","fa":"پنج کلمه"},"text":"The email from Omar arrived at 6:40 a.m. The subject line was empty. The message was five words long.\n\n\"Need 3 drivers. ASAP. Omar.\"\n\nLeyla read it three times. Was he angry? Was this normal in Dubai? She did not know, and that was the problem. Which drivers? For which route? ASAP meant today, or this week?\n\nShe could answer in the same style, but it felt wrong. She could also write a very long, nervous reply. She chose a third way.\n\n\"Dear Omar, thank you for your message. I'm writing to confirm what you need. Could you tell me which route the three drivers will work on, and when you'd like them to start? I was wondering if you could also send me the licence type, so I can check the CVs we already have. If I have this by the end of the day, I can send you a shortlist on Thursday. Kind regards, Leyla.\"\n\nTwenty minutes later Omar called her instead. \"Sorry,\" he said. \"I wrote it on my phone in a taxi. Cargo trucks, Sharjah route, start on the first. Class C licence.\"\n\nLeyla wrote it all down. \"That's all I needed,\" she said. She noticed that he had said sorry. Nobody had asked him to.","vocab":[{"word":"subject line","en":"The short title at the top of an email.","tr":"konu satırı","fa":"موضوع ایمیل (خط عنوان)"},{"word":"route","en":"The road a driver follows from A to B.","tr":"güzergâh","fa":"مسیر حمل؛ مسیری که راننده از مبدأ تا مقصد می‌رود"},{"word":"licence","en":"An official paper that allows you to do something, such as drive.","tr":"ehliyet, lisans","fa":"گواهینامه؛ مجوز رسمی"},{"word":"shortlist","en":"A short list of the best candidates.","tr":"kısa liste","fa":"فهرست منتخب؛ فهرست کوتاه بهترین متقاضیان"},{"word":"nervous","en":"A little afraid or worried.","tr":"gergin, tedirgin","fa":"نگران؛ مضطرب"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"Why was Omar's first email a problem?","options":["It gave no details, so Leyla could not act","It was too long","It was sent to the wrong person"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"Which sentence is a correct polite request?","options":["Could you to tell me the route?","Could you tell me the route?","Could you telling me the route?"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Why did Leyla add \"by the end of the day\"?","options":["To give a deadline and a reason to answer","To sound angry","To end the email"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"How did Omar probably feel on the phone?","options":["A little embarrassed that his email was so short","Proud of the email","Bored with the project"],"correct":0}],"notice":{"en":"Omar's email is five words long. Watch how Leyla turns her questions into requests he can answer quickly.","tr":"Omar'ın e-postası beş kelime. Leyla'nın sorularını, onun hızlıca cevaplayabileceği ricalara nasıl çevirdiğine dikkat et.","fa":"ایمیل عمر پنج کلمه است. دقت کن لیلا چطور سؤال‌هایش را به درخواست‌هایی تبدیل می‌کند که عمر بتواند زود جوابشان را بدهد."},"bridge":{"en":"Leyla's reply used polite openers and a deadline. Next: see how they work.","tr":"Leyla'nın cevabında kibar başlangıç kalıpları ve bir son tarih vardı. Sırada: nasıl çalıştıklarını gör.","fa":"جواب لیلا چند شروع مؤدبانه و یک مهلت داشت. قدم بعد: ببین چطور کار می‌کنند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-1-2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","topic":{"en":"Making a Polite Request by Phone","tr":"Telefonda Kibar Bir Rica","fa":"درخواست مؤدبانه پشت تلفن"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a time you got a message that was too short. What did you do?","tr":"Çok kısa bir mesaj aldığın bir zamanı düşün. Ne yaptın?","fa":"یک بار را به یاد بیاور که پیامی خیلی کوتاه به دستت رسید. چه کردی؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Ask a manager to send you the details of a new vacancy.","tr":"Bir yöneticiden yeni bir açık pozisyonun ayrıntılarını göndermesini iste.","fa":"از یک مدیر بخواه جزئیات یک موقعیت شغلی تازه را برایت بفرستد."},{"en":"Ask a colleague to confirm a meeting time. Give a reason.","tr":"Bir iş arkadaşından toplantı saatini teyit etmesini iste. Bir sebep ver.","fa":"از یک همکار بخواه ساعت جلسه را تأیید کند. دلیلش را هم بگو."},{"en":"Ask a supplier to reply by the end of the day.","tr":"Bir tedarikçiden gün sonuna kadar yanıt vermesini iste.","fa":"از یک تأمین‌کننده بخواه تا آخر امروز جواب بدهد."}],"followups":[{"en":"Say each request twice: once bluntly, once politely. Notice the difference.","tr":"Her ricayı iki kez söyle: önce sert, sonra kibar. Aradaki farka dikkat et.","fa":"هر درخواست را دو بار بگو: یک بار رُک و بی‌مقدمه، یک بار مؤدبانه. به تفاوتش دقت کن."},{"en":"Now make one polite request you really need to make at work this week.","tr":"Şimdi bu hafta işte gerçekten yapman gereken bir ricayı nazikçe söyle.","fa":"حالا درخواستی را که این هفته واقعاً در کارت داری مؤدبانه بگو."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"I was wondering if you could...","meaning":{"en":"Very polite request.","tr":"Çok kibar rica.","fa":"درخواست بسیار مؤدبانه"}},{"phrase":"Would you mind sending...","meaning":{"en":"Polite; followed by -ing.","tr":"Kibar; arkasından -ing gelir.","fa":"مؤدبانه؛ بعد از آن فعل ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید"}},{"phrase":"by the end of the day","meaning":{"en":"A clear deadline.","tr":"Net bir son tarih.","fa":"یک مهلت مشخص"}}],"culture":{"en":"Some workplaces, such as many in the Persian Gulf and in fast-moving logistics, write short, direct messages and do not mean to be rude. In the UK, very short emails can feel cold. When unsure, add one polite opener and one clear deadline.","tr":"Basra Körfezi'ndeki birçok işyeri ve hızlı lojistik sektörü gibi bazı ortamlarda kısa ve doğrudan mesajlar yazılır; bu kabalık anlamına gelmez. Birleşik Krallık'ta çok kısa e-postalar soğuk algılanabilir. Emin değilsen bir kibar giriş ve net bir son tarih ekle.","fa":"در بعضی محیط‌های کاری، مثل بسیاری از شرکت‌های حاشیه‌ی خلیج فارس و شرکت‌های پرشتاب لجستیک، پیام‌ها را کوتاه و مستقیم می‌نویسند و قصد بی‌احترامی ندارند. در بریتانیا اما ایمیل خیلی کوتاه ممکن است سرد به نظر برسد. اگر مطمئن نیستی، یک جمله‌ی شروع مؤدبانه و یک مهلت روشن اضافه کن."},"model":"Hi Omar, it's Leyla from HR. I'm calling about the driver vacancy. It's a bit urgent, so could you send me the details of the route by the end of the day? I was wondering if you could also tell me the licence type, because I want to check the CVs we already have. Would you mind sending the start date too? Then I can send you a shortlist on Thursday. Thanks a lot.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I used 'Could you' with a bare verb.","tr":"'Could you'yu yalın fiille kullandım.","fa":"«Could you» را با شکل ساده‌ی فعل به کار بردم."},{"en":"I used 'Would you mind' + -ing or 'I was wondering if'.","tr":"'Would you mind' + -ing ya da 'I was wondering if' kullandım.","fa":"از «⁨Would you mind⁩» با ⁨-ing⁩ یا از «⁨I was wondering if⁩» استفاده کردم."},{"en":"Every request had a reason or a deadline.","tr":"Her ricanın bir nedeni ya da son tarihi vardı.","fa":"هر درخواستم یک دلیل یا مهلت داشت."},{"en":"Round 3 fitted in 45 seconds.","tr":"3. tur 45 saniyeye sığdı.","fa":"دور سوم در ۴۵ ثانیه تمام شد."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-w","title":{"en":"Leyla's reply to Omar","tr":"Leyla'nın Omar'a cevabı","fa":"جواب لیلا به عمر"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Omar wrote: \"Need 3 drivers. ASAP.\" Write Leyla's reply: say you need two details, ask politely, and give a deadline.","tr":"Omar şunu yazdı: \"Need 3 drivers. ASAP.\" Leyla'nın yanıtını yaz: iki bilgiye ihtiyacın olduğunu söyle, kibarca iste ve bir son tarih ver.","fa":"عمر نوشته است: «⁨Need 3 drivers. ASAP.⁩» جواب لیلا را بنویس: بگو دو چیز را باید بدانی، آن‌ها را مؤدبانه بخواه و یک مهلت تعیین کن."},"model":"Dear Omar, thank you for your message. I'm writing to ask about the three drivers. Could you confirm which route they will work on? I was wondering if you could also send me the licence type. If I have this by the end of the day, I can send you a shortlist on Thursday. I've attached the job description we used last time. Kind regards, Leyla","frame":"Dear ___, thank you for ___. I'm writing to ___. Could you tell me ___? I was wondering if you could also ___. If I have this by ___, I can ___. Kind regards, ___","words":[{"word":"confirm"},{"word":"by the end of the day"},{"word":"I was wondering if"}],"minWords":45,"minSentences":4,"rubric":["Task done: two questions + deadline","Organised: purpose, request, deadline, close","Language: Could you + base verb; I was wondering if + statement","Tone: polite but clear; no ASAP-only commands"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: iki soru + son tarih","Düzen: amaç, rica, son tarih, kapanış","Dil: Could you + yalın fiil; I was wondering if + düz cümle","Üslup: kibar ama net; yalnızca \"ASAP\" diyen emirler yok"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: دو سؤال به‌همراه مهلت","نظم: هدف، درخواست، مهلت، پایان","زبان: Could you با شکل ساده‌ی فعل؛ I was wondering if با جمله‌ی خبری","لحن: مؤدب ولی روشن؛ بدون دستورهایی که فقط «ASAP» می‌گویند"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"Why you are writing","tr":"Neden yazdığın","fa":"دلیل نوشتنت"},"find":["i'm writing to","i am writing to","i'm writing about","thank you for"],"sample":"ask about the three drivers"},{"t":{"en":"Your first question","tr":"İlk sorun","fa":"سؤال اولت"},"find":["could you","can you","would you"],"sample":"which route they will work on"},{"t":{"en":"Your second question","tr":"İkinci sorun","fa":"سؤال دومت"},"find":["i was wondering if","would you mind","also"],"sample":"the licence type"},{"t":{"en":"Your deadline","tr":"Son tarihin","fa":"مهلتت"},"find":["by","before","deadline"],"sample":"by the end of the day, so the shortlist can go on Thursday"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-p","title":{"en":"Leyla at 6:40 a.m.","tr":"Sabah 6.40'ta Leyla","fa":"لیلا، ساعت ۶:۴۰ صبح"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Leyla at 6:40 a.m., reading Omar's five-word email. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: how does it feel, and what do you guess about Omar?","tr":"Sabah 6.40'ta Omar'ın beş kelimelik e-postasını okuyan Leyla'sın. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: nasıl hissediyorsun ve Omar hakkında ne tahmin ediyorsun?","fa":"تو لیلا هستی. ساعت ۶:۴۰ صبح است و ایمیل پنج‌کلمه‌ای عمر را می‌خوانی. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: چه حسی داری و درباره‌ی عمر چه حدسی می‌زنی؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-1-2-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-1-2","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-1-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Could you ___ the interview dates, please?","options":["to confirm","confirm","confirming"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"confirm: 'Could you' + plain verb. 'To confirm' and 'confirming' don't follow could.","tr":"confirm: 'Could you' + yalın fiil. 'To confirm' ve 'confirming' could'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"confirm درست است، چون بعد از Could you فعل ساده می‌آید. to confirm و confirming بعد از could نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"hr-1-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Would you mind ___ me the list?","options":["send","sending","to send"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"sending: 'Would you mind' takes -ing. 'Send' and 'to send' don't follow mind.","tr":"sending: 'Would you mind' -ing alır. 'Send' ve 'to send' mind'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"sending درست است، چون بعد از Would you mind فعل ing‌دار می‌آید. send و to send بعد از mind نمی‌آیند."},"hint2":{"en":"Would you mind works like I don’t mind: which verb form follows it?","tr":"Would you mind, I don’t mind gibi çalışır: Ondan sonra fiilin hangi biçimi gelir?","fa":"⁨Would you mind⁩ مثل ⁨I don’t mind⁩ است: بعدش فعل با چه شکلی می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-1-2","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence gives a deadline?","options":["If I have this by Thursday, I can reply on Friday.","I'd appreciate it if you could send me this.","I'm writing to ask about Thursday."],"correct":0,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'If I have this by Thursday, I can reply on Friday' gives a date and the reason for it. The other two have no deadline.","tr":"'If I have this by Thursday, I can reply on Friday' bir tarih ve nedenini verir. Diğer ikisinde son tarih yoktur.","fa":"«If I have this by Thursday, I can reply on Friday» تاریخ و دلیلش را می‌گوید. دو جمله‌ی دیگر مهلت ندارند."}},{"from":"hr-1-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"At the moment I ___ on the hiring plan.","options":["work","am working","works"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"am working: 'at the moment' is now, so am + -ing. 'Work' is a habit, and 'works' doesn't agree with I.","tr":"am working: 'at the moment' şimdidir, bu yüzden am + -ing. 'Work' alışkanlıktır; 'works' I ile uyuşmaz.","fa":"am working درست است، چون at the moment یعنی الان و am و فعل ing‌دار لازم است. work عادت است و works با I جور نیست."}},{"from":"hr-1-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"The HR team ___ a new office in Istanbul.","options":["has","is having","have"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"has: owning an office is a state, so present simple with -s for one team. 'Is having' is wrong for a state, and 'have' is plural.","tr":"has: bir ofise sahip olmak durumdur; tek bir ekip için -s'li geniş zaman. 'Is having' durum için yanlıştır; 'have' çoğuldur.","fa":"⁨has⁩ درست است، چون داشتن دفتر حالت است و برای یک تیم حال ساده با ⁨-s⁩ می‌آید. ⁨is having⁩ برای حالت غلط است و ⁨have⁩ جمع است."}},{"from":"hr-1-1","kind":"mcq","prompt":"\"I report to the HR director\" means...","options":["She is my manager.","I write reports about her.","I work for her every weekend."],"correct":0,"point":3,"why":{"en":"'I report to the HR director' means she is my manager. It has nothing to do with writing reports or weekend work.","tr":"'I report to the HR director' onun yöneticim olduğu demektir. Rapor yazmak ya da hafta sonu çalışmakla ilgisi yoktur.","fa":"«I report to the HR director» یعنی او مدیر من است. ربطی به گزارش نوشتن یا کار آخر هفته ندارد."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
